From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 15:46:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Hide empty image row in hero-banner variant

The hero-banner carries no image but needs an empty image row so its
content columns align to the hero model (image, then text) for md2jcr.
Hide that empty first row so it doesn't render as a blank gap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 blocks/hero/hero.css | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/blocks/hero/hero.css b/blocks/hero/hero.css
index 75eaa48..c9465f3 100644
--- a/blocks/hero/hero.css
+++ b/blocks/hero/hero.css
@@ -159,6 +159,11 @@
   background-color: var(--hero-banner-bg);
 }
 
+/* the banner carries no image; hide the empty image row kept for model alignment */
+.hero-banner > div:first-child:not(:only-child) {
+  display: none;
+}
+
 .hero-banner h1,
 .hero-banner h2 {
   max-width: 900px;
-- 
